    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0466" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.01/5–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-23T14:00:00+03:00">May 23, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1715. My Brit colleague<anchor n="6" xml:id="d457-f1"/> has received note from
                        Vyshinski<anchor n="7" xml:id="d457-f2"/> in reply to an inquiry made by
                    Clark Kerr on April 16 stating that the <pb facs="0467" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/>
                    Czech Foreign Ministry has informed the Soviet Govt that the Czech Govt has been
                    transferred from Bratislava to Prague; that the Czech Govt has decided on the
                    transfer in the near future of the Allied Diplomatic Reps from London; and that
                    the Soviet Govt does not object to this decision.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d457-f3"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 1715; rptd to London for Schoenfeld as 220.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d457-f1" n="6" xml:id="d457-f1-content">
                <p>The British Chargé, Frank Roberts.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d457-f2" n="7" xml:id="d457-f2-content">
                <p>Andrey Yanuaryevich Vyshinsky, First Deputy People’s Commissar for Foreign
                    Affairs of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d457-f3" n="8" xml:id="d457-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram Zecho 57, May 16, from London, reported that Minister Ripka, who was to
                    leave London for Prague the following day, had stated that it was definite that
                    the United States Embassy group could proceed to Prague when ready
                    (124.60F/5–1645).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
